{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":493805,"name":"Kamil Šenk","username":"Kamil_Senk","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/k/ee59a6/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T10:37:13.579Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493805-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493805-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493805-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493805-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy Grok Bot has completely stopped working and can’t connect to any network. It worked reliably on my home computer, but then I tried to get Grok up and running on the corporate network at work, and even though the IT administrator says everything is set up exactly as you describe in your instructions, it just doesn’t work. I’ve tried everything. According to the IT administrator, Grok isn’t even visible as attempting to connect.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI don’t know what to do; please advise and help.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKamil\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493805-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493805-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry to close and open the app, reconnect?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493805-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493805-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/3/9/39b834db6bd12fd7585bda8a59d32aca48b78c76.png\" data-download-h