99fe110b2_2_904x750.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/6/7/6770005f67a185e75c261bc68e6d41999fe110b2_2_1206x1000.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"AFAEAF\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eissue2.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1552×1286 71.7 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493805-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493805-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493805-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493805-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot windows app v.0.55.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493805-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493805-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo other info\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493805-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493805-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T10:37:22.767Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":44,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":221.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":172003,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-connection-issue-reconnecting-on-corporate-network-and-not-working-in-mobile-app","display_username":"Kamil Šenk","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138358,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-connection-issue-reconnecting-on-corporate-network-and-not-working-in-mobile-app/172003/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":495686,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-19T12:05:48.355Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey Kamil, thanks for the detailed report and the screenshots. They show “Reconnecting to your computer” and “Couldn’t check for updates”, and this looks like your work PC can’t reach our servers, not an issue with the Bots themselves. Your Bots and data are fine, so please don’t press Recover or Reset. It won’t help and can just make the state confusing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKey point for your IT admin: allowing domains on the proxy isn’t enough. The app needs the PC itself to be able to open a direct outbound HTTPS connection (port 443) to our domains, with TLS/SSL inspection disabled for them. That’s why the proxy might not even see the connection attempts. Domains (full list in the docs):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e*.cursor.sh\u003c/code\u003e (including \u003ccode\u003eapi2.cursor.sh\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e*.cursorapi.com\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ecursor.com\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003edownloads.cursor.com\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDocs: \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/enterprise/network-configuration\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eNetwork Configuration | Cursor Docs\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/grok-bot/proxies\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eConfigure TLS-inspecting proxies | Cursor Docs\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo figure out what’s being blocked, please run this on the work PC and send the results:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen PowerShell (Start \u0026gt; type “PowerShell” \u0026gt; Enter).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ecurl.exe -v https://api2.cursor.sh\u003c/code\u003e and copy the lines with “Connected to”, “issuer:” or “Failed”/“Could not”. On a normal work network you’ll see “issuer: … Amazon”, on proxy-only setups you often see “Failed to connect”.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003enslookup api2.cursor.sh\u003c/code\u003e and copy the output.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConnect the same PC to your phone hotspot for a minute, open Grok Bot, and tell me if it connects.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOn your phone, open Grok Bot first on mobile data (Wi-Fi off), then on office Wi-Fi, and tell me where it works.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf it works on the hotspot but not on the office network, the fix is on the network side (direct HTTPS from the PC to the domains above). If it doesn’t work even on the hotspot, tell me and we’ll look at the PC itself (antivirus or endpoint security can also block the app). Let me know what the tests show.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-19T12:05:48.355Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":172003,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-connection-issue-reconnecting-on-corporate-network-and-not-working-in-mobile-app","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://cursor.com/docs/grok-bot/proxies","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Configure TLS-inspecting proxies | Cursor Docs","clicks":0},{"url":"https://cursor.com/docs/enterprise/network-configuration","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Network Configuration | Cursor Docs","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-connection-issue-reconnecting-on-corporate-network-and-not-working-in-mobile-app/172003/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[493805,495686]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,4],[2,2]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot connection issue (reconnecting on corporate network) and not working in mobile app","id":172003,"title":"Grok